    "text": "Curable Breach (a) (b) In the event DISTRIBUTOR fails to pay for Product when due in accordance with Paragraph 4; or sells PRODUCT outside of DISTRIBUTOR’S AUTHORIZED CHANNEL OF TRADE; COMPANY shall give DISTRIBUTOR five (5) business days written notice within which DISTRIBUTOR may cure its failure of performance by making all payments due, and may cure unauthorized selling by ceasing to sell to unauthorized customers. If DISTRIBUTOR fails to cure such failure of performance within said five (5) day period, COMPANY may thereafter terminate this Agreement and DISTRIBUTOR will have no further right to cure; provided, further, that the parties agree that should any such failure(s) occur more than two (2) times during any twelve (12) month period, COMPANY may immediately terminate this Agreement upon written notice to DISTRIBUTOR and DISTRIBUTOR will have no further right to cure."
