    "text": "DISTRIBUTOR non agency relationship with Company Neither COMPANY nor DISTRIBUTOR shall have any authority to employ any person on behalf of the other. Each party shall have (as between the parties) the exclusive right to select, engage, fix the compensation of, discharge, and otherwise to manage, supervise, and control the person hired by it and shall, with respect to all such persons, perform all obligations and discharge all liabilities imposed upon employers under any governing law or regulation. Without limitation, DISTRIBUTOR: (a) shall be solely responsible for the conduct, direction, and operation of its activities, including but not limited to the conduct, direction, and operation of the activities of its employees and subcontractors, in connection with its business and the performance of its obligations under this Agreement; (b) shall make no contract, representation or warranty nor incur any obligation for or in the name of or binding upon COMPANY and shall not list its place of business as COMPANY’S office but only may identify itself as COMPANY’S independent contractor for the distribution of the PRODUCTS; (c) shall provide and maintain at its own expense suitable equipment for the delivery of the PRODUCTS; (d) shall not pledge COMPANY’S credit or extend credit in COMPANY’S name; and (e) shall indemnify and defend COMPANY against, and save it harmless from, any claims which may arise as a result of any representation by DISTRIBUTOR that it has authority to act on behalf of COMPANY or to bind COMPANY to any obligations whatsoever."
